                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>"Chiral Drugs and Chiral Synthesis Reactions" is an elective course designed to expand and enhance undergraduate students' expertise in organic chemistry. The curriculum focuses on the fundamental concepts of chiral synthesis reactions, methods for determining enantiomeric purity and absolute configuration of chiral compounds, as well as the primary pathways for obtaining chiral compounds. Through this course, students will acquire a foundational understanding of the diverse synthetic methodologies and fundamental principles of chiral construction. Case studies are incorporated to illustrate the application of these principles in the synthesis of chiral drugs.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
